title: "RAGentGuard: Cross-Stage Provenance Monitoring for Retrieval-Augmented Generation Agents"
version: 0.2.1
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/LeoTTTPhat/RAGentGuard"
abstract: >
  RAGentGuard is a runtime monitor for retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)
  agents. It labels every segment of content with an integrity level, gives
  derived content (tool feedback, memory notes, messages between agents) the
  least trusted label of its sources, attributes each proposed tool call to the
  segments it came from, and gates side-effecting calls at dispatch, using
  content detectors as evidence. This release contains the experiment code and
  raw outputs of the accompanying manuscript.
keywords:
  - RAG security
  - prompt injection
  - taint tracking
  - LLM agents
  - adversarial ML
